        "cap": "2 half-circles make a circle. 3 triangles make a trapezoid. 2 trapezoids make a hexagon."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "Shapes can be put together to make new shapes, and new shapes can be put together again."
      },
      {
        "t": "why",
        "html": "When pieces fit with no gaps and no overlaps, the outside edge is a new shape. You can trace it to name it."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Two squares",
        "q": "What shape do 2 squares side by side make?",
        "steps": [
          "The outside edge has 4 straight sides and 4 square corners.",
          "It is longer than it is tall.",
          "It is a rectangle."
        ],
        "a": "A rectangle"
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "<b>For grown-ups:</b> Pattern blocks, paper cut-outs or toast cut into triangles all work for building new shapes."
      },
      {
        "t": "try"
      }
